{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Target platform is Spring XD (built on Spring Framework 6 / Spring Integration), with Java 17+.",
    "Message bus abstraction is assumed to be pluggable (RabbitMQ as the primary target, Redis as a secondary case), with a clean provider interface used to add destroy/cleanup hooks.",
    "U1 and U2 are implemented together as a unified 'stream-destroy cleanup' lifecycle that removes both actively-bound and stale queues/topics/exchanges for the destroyed stream's modules.",
    "U3 is implemented as an in-place 'redeploy' flow that tears down only the bus bindings and redeploys modules with new properties, avoiding the need for a full destroy/create cycle.",
    "U4 is implemented as a deployment-manifest loader that reads a properties/YAML file (in addition to the existing inline --properties), with merge semantics (file values act as defaults, inline values override).",
    "U6 uses Spring Integration's global wiretap pattern, configured dynamically from the deployment properties (module.<name>.trace or module.*.trace) so the same code path supports single-module and wildcard tracing.",
    "U7 reuses the wiretap mechanism from U6 plus a 'side channel' declaration on the stream DSL to create additional named channels beyond input/output, used for in-flow tap/tracking.",
    "U5 is delivered as a set of curated reference architecture markdown docs plus minimal runnable POCs (no full enterprise-ready architectures).",
    "U8 is implemented as a runnable Spring XD stream + simple analytics sink/aggregator reading the NYC taxi dataset from a public source, with documentation of how to run it.",
    "Testing strategy: JUnit 5 unit tests for each module, plus integration tests using an embedded/test message bus (or a containerized broker) for stream lifecycle and tracing scenarios."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced Java/Spring developer performs all work; familiarity with Spring Integration, Spring XD, and AMQP/RabbitMQ is assumed.",
    "The existing Spring XD codebase, build system (Gradle), and CI are already in place; no bootstrapping of repositories is required.",
    "A test message broker (e.g., embedded Qpid or Dockerized RabbitMQ) is available for integration testing.",
    "All estimates represent productive development effort, not calendar duration; no meetings, vacation, or onboarding are included.",
    "No new external systems (e.g., a new datastore, a new message bus provider) are introduced beyond what Spring XD already supports.",
    "The NYC taxi dataset is publicly downloadable; no special data acquisition or licensing work is required for U8.",
    "Reference architectures (U5) are scoped as 'first-step' design captures, not production-ready reference implementations.",
    "No migration of existing user data or streams is required; new behaviors are opt-in via deployment properties/CLI flags."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and technical design",
      "activity_description": "Review the existing Spring XD stream lifecycle, deployment, and message bus code paths; produce a technical design that covers the destroy/cleanup hooks, in-place redeploy, manifest loader, tracing/wiretap, and side-channel mechanisms; align with the eight user stories."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement stream-destroy cleanup of message bus resources (U1 + U2)",
      "activity_description": "Add a destroy-time cleanup hook to the stream lifecycle that deletes queues, topics, and exchanges associated with the stream's modules, including stale resources from prior failed destroys."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement edit/redeploy of a deployed stream (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Extend the deploy command/flow to support updating the deployment properties of an already-deployed stream by undeploying and redeploying in place, without requiring destroy + recreate of the stream definition."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement deployment manifest loaded from a file (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Add support for the deploy command to read deployment properties from a file path (in addition to inline --properties), with a clear merge/override policy between file and inline values."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement inline trace deployment properties via wiretap (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Parse module.<name>.trace and module.*.trace from deployment properties and apply the Spring Integration global wiretap to the targeted modules' channels so messages are intercepted for logging/notification."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement arbitrary side channels in a stream flow (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Extend the stream DSL/module model to allow declaring additional named channels beyond input/output, create the corresponding bus resources, and expose them so a wiretap/tap can be used to track module progress."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Author Spring XD reference architecture documentation (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Capture domain-specific reference architectures as design docs and small runnable POCs (e.g., real-time analytics, ETL, event-driven microservices) for field engineers to use as starting points."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Build NYC taxi trips demo/evaluation application (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a runnable Spring XD stream that ingests the DEBS 2015 NYC taxi trip reports, performs simple real-time analytics, and documents how to run and evaluate it."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Unit testing",
      "activity_description": "Write JUnit 5 unit tests for the new lifecycle hooks, redeploy flow, manifest loader, wiretap property parsing, side-channel creation, and reference-architecture POC building blocks."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Write end-to-end integration tests against an embedded/test message broker covering: destroy cleanup of queues/topics, in-place redeploy with new properties, manifest-from-file deployment, trace/wiretap message capture, side-channel tap, and the taxi demo stream."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "User-facing documentation and release notes",
      "activity_description": "Update the Spring XD reference documentation with new CLI flags, deployment property formats, side-channel DSL syntax, reference architecture index, and the taxi demo runbook; add release notes summarizing the increment."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 296
  }
}
```

